package {{package}}

// From the files of project/, ritsu makes go/ (the Go code of the request types, their rules and
// dates, and the gate) and requests/ (what the server reads, and the vectors the tests run). Run it
// again after changing them:
//
//	go generate ./...
//
// For CI, the same line with --check writes nothing, and fails when go/ or requests/ is not what
// project/ makes. --lang is the language of the sentences in the code that is made; the line names it,
// so that it is the same whoever runs it. --catalog is the ID of the catalog of the project's screens:
// make it a URL you own, the same in every environment.
//
//go:generate ritsu gen project --root project --target go --target requests --catalog {{catalog}} --module {{module}}/go --out . --lang {{lang}}
